298: | Year 3 mid-year (week 17, days 33 and 34) | 2 | 1 | 1 | Samples unit 1 in its own year: a fresh improvisation in groups of five from a new scenario card, marked live: characters and a place invented (TH:Cr1.1.3a), the agreed way the characters move and speak (TH:Cr1.1.3c) and the scene fitted to a two-minute limit (TH:Cr3.1.3a); and a kept card filled while another group plays: which of two ideas the student's group kept and why it made the scene stronger (TH:Cr2.1.3b). Unit 2's showing and written record (days 30 and 31) is carried unscored; no exercise-set task repeats. Respond on day 34. |
299: | Year 3 year-end (week 27, days 53 and 54) | 3 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 1 and 2: a fresh two-line scene played after one rehearsal run, marked live: body and voice explored for the character (TH:Cr3.1.3b, unit 2); a kept reflection line written after the run (TH:Pr6.1.3a, unit 1); and an audience card filled while another group plays: how the student connects with a character's feeling (TH:Re8.1.3c, unit 2). Unit 3's showing and written record (days 50 and 51) is carried unscored. Unit 4 is assessed by its own showing. Respond on day 54. |
300: | Year 4 mid-year (week 17, days 97 and 98) | 6 | 1 | 1 | Samples unit 5: a fresh scene from a new given-circumstances card, shown to the class as audience, marked live: the story fits its given circumstances (TH:Cr1.1.4a), a character moves to fit them (TH:Cr1.1.4c) and the group's work shown to classmates (TH:Pr6.1.4a); and a kept jobs list for the fresh scene (TH:Cr2.1.4b). Unit 6's showing and written record (days 94 and 95) is carried unscored. Respond on day 98. |
