304: 
305: Each check day: set-up 3, warm-up 5, six groups of five play the fresh scene for about 4 minutes each (24) while the
306: others are the audience and fill the card the check uses, close 4; the teacher marks one group at a time and reads
307: the cards after the session. Every student's evidence is collected once in a window; no artifact is scored twice.
308: Days above are band course days (year 4 starts on day 65, year 5 on day 129).
309: 
310: ## Cross-subject
311: 
312: Three theater rows of grades 3 to 5 carry a cross_subject lean on English language arts (data/progressions/arts.csv):
313: ela:RL.3.3 (th-g3-story), ela:SL.4.4 (th-g4-actor) and ela:RL.5.3 (th-g5-story). All are core courses (lesson 32);
314: each is practiced here, not owned, and the theater unit does not reteach it (STANDARD.md 6).
315: 
316: ### English language arts, grade 3 (same year)
317: 
318: | Used here | Lean | Where ELA teaches it | If ELA has not taught it yet |
319: |---|---|---|---|
320: | Unit 4, days 55 to 64 (weeks 28 to 32 of year 3): how a character's actions move the story, in the play made from the tale (th-g3-story) | RL.3.3 | ELA grade 3 unit 1 (days 1 to 39) | Taught by then. If a school runs ELA late, the story map's "because" arrows carry the characters' actions and the teacher models one before the students try |
321: 
322: ### English language arts, grade 4 (same year)
323: 
324: | Used here | Lean | Where ELA teaches it | If ELA has not taught it yet |
325: |---|---|---|---|
326: | Unit 6, band days 81 to 96 (days 17 to 32 of year 4, weeks 9 to 16): speaking clearly in a character's voice at a pace the audience can follow (th-g4-actor) | SL.4.4 | ELA grade 4 unit 1 (days 1 to 38) | Taught by then. If not, the theater unit marks only the character's body and voice choices, never a whole spoken report, and the warm-up card shows "to the back wall, one word at a time" |
327: 
328: ### English language arts, grade 5 (same year)
329: 
330: | Used here | Lean | Where ELA teaches it | If ELA has not taught it yet |
331: |---|---|---|---|
332: | Unit 12, band days 183 to 192 (days 55 to 64 of year 5, weeks 28 to 32): comparing characters and events across three tellings before the play is made (th-g5-story) | RL.5.3 | ELA grade 5 unit 1 (days 1 to 41) | Taught by then. If not, the comparison chart gives the three tellings' characters and events in rows, and the teacher models one comparison first |
333: 
334: Written audience-journal entries and defended responses (units 2, 6, 10) practice opinion writing with a reason
335: (W.3.1, W.4.1, W.5.1): practiced, not owned. ELA teaches them in grade 3 unit 3 (days 81 to 119), grade 4 unit 3
336: (days 81 to 119) and grade 5 unit 3 (days 84 to 123). If ELA has not taught them yet, the response card gives the
337: frame ("I think ___ because ___. I saw it when ___.") and at most two written items a student. Talk about scenes and
338: the critique practice collaborative conversation (SL.3.1, SL.4.1, SL.5.1): practiced, not owned; the group agreements
339: and critique-protocol cards show the turn-taking steps.
340: 
341: ### Science, social studies and mathematics, grades 3 to 5
342: 
343: No lean either way. Unit 7's light and sound cues and unit 11's cues sit near grade 4 science's light and sound
344: work; the theater units name light and sound only by their use in a scene and ask no science explanation. Units 3, 7
345: and 11 take their community and problem facts from fact cards Curio Class writes, and units 8, 11 and 12 teach the
346: setting of each work themselves, on work cards (bar criterion 7). No unit asks for number work (lesson 13): the
347: two-minute limit of unit 1 is kept on the teacher's timer as a pace cue, and no student measures or counts time.
348: 
349: ## For the lead
350: 
351: 1. **After-core check weeks.** This frame's checks stay off every core check week: mid-year weeks 17 (years 3 and 4)
352:    and 18 (year 5); year-end week 27 (years 3 and 5) and 26 (year 4). Chosen by unit load, not to dodge other
353:    after-core courses; any sharing with other after-core courses in `frame.py calendar` is left for the lead's one
354:    calendar pass.
355: 2. **Once-a-week respond sessions.** On the once-a-week path the year-end respond session falls in week 28 in year 3
356:    and week 27 in year 4, which hold social studies year-end checks in grades 3 and 4; they are respond sessions, not
357:    checks, but the calendar pass should decide whether the rule counts them.
358: 3. **Theater national time figure.** STANDARD.md 3.4 says the theater association gives no minutes; the second-model
359:    prework read (docs/reviews/prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md) cites the Educational Theatre Association's
360:    opportunity-to-learn standards (schooltheatre.org). This job did no download. Pick: read that document at source
361:    once (it may be a file, which Desk q-fix-downloads-1 allows) and, if it gives an elementary figure, add it with the
362:    gap to this frame's Days bullet and STANDARD.md 3.4.
363: 4. **Leave-out and play-acting.** As in theater K to 2: every unit is play-acting, so leaving out play-acting leaves
364:    out the course. No change asked; noted so the course page wording matches.
365: 5. **Row changes** (listed in the final message): twelve "Assessed by" notes name one form narrower than their ids;
366:    the frame's id-by-id evidence lines govern meanwhile.
367: 6. **Supplies ceiling (money, for Cory).** Provisional costs: $35 (year 3), $40 (year 4), $30 (year 5) a class of 30,
368:    all optional beside a free path. Pick: a ceiling of $40 a class a year for 3 to 5 theater, with every unit's
369:    free path kept.
370: 7. **Sensitivity choices made here.** Three item-level calls, each read first by the sensitivity agent: unit 7 tells
371:    the old Peter Pan stereotype only in Larissa FastHorse's own words and shows no old images; unit 11 names the
372:    Kamiriithu closing and Ng�cg�c wa Thiong'o's 1978 detention in one plain sentence each; unit 12 uses the Zuni
373:    Poor Turkey Girl only if Zuni Pueblo's own heritage sources treat it as open to be told, else swaps it.

