**Problem:** The unit teaches and checks moments when characters decide something within the plot. `TH:Re7.1.2a` concerns recognizing artistic choices during guided drama. The local words file preserves the distinction by naming artists, but the progression note and frame lose it. The next frame then expects students to explain artists�?T decisions. See the [official theater standards, PDF page 6](https://www.nationalartsstandards.org/sites/default/files/2021-11/Theatre%20at%20a%20Glance%20-%20new%20copyright%20info.pdf#page=6).

**Why it matters:** A child could satisfy every stated item without noticing a performer�?Ts choice of voice, movement or delivery.

**Exact fix:**

- Replace the unit�?Ts question ending with: �?oWhen do performers choose how to show a character?�??
- Teach recognition through two versions of a moment, such as the same line delivered with different voices or gestures.
- Replace the audience-card item with: �?oMark the moment a performer chose a voice, movement or gesture; point to or describe that choice.�??
- Make the year-end sample and outgoing seam use that same action.
- Rewrite the relevant `th-g2-notice` note around performers�?T artistic choices. Keep character problem-solving under `TH:Re9.1.2c`.

No ownership change is needed.

