Each row of years 7 and 8 assumes the year before's row in its thread (one grade back), so it opens as a retrieval
task inside day 2 of its unit.

| Thread | Year 6 row (unit, course days) | Year 7 row that picks it up (unit) | Year 8 row that picks it up (unit) | What changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Imagining | th-g6-imagine (unit 2, days 19 to 32) | th-g7-imagine (unit 6): several viewpoints weighed, a choice defended | th-g8-imagine (unit 10) retrieves th-g7-imagine (unit 6, days 83 to 96): research builds an original idea | Fixes tested, then viewpoints defended, then research-built ideas |
| Showing | th-g6-show (unit 4, days 49 to 62) | th-g7-show (unit 8): respect for each role, focused rehearsal, every rehearsal kept | th-g8-show (unit 12) retrieves th-g7-show (unit 8, days 113 to 126): rotating leads, rework by runs, a polished staging | An adapted informal showing, then a rehearsed showing, then a polished staging |
| Actor | th-g6-actor (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | th-g7-actor (unit 5): goals tried, inner thoughts written | th-g8-actor (unit 9) retrieves th-g7-actor (unit 5, days 65 to 82): tactics against an obstacle, polished traits | Given circumstances, then goals and an inner life, then tactics and motives |
| Design | th-g6-design (unit 3, days 35 to 48) | th-g7-design (unit 7): several elements chosen and weighed | th-g8-design (unit 11) retrieves th-g7-design (unit 7, days 99 to 112): the real venue, simple technology | One fix tried, then many elements weighed, then a combined design for the venue |
| Story | th-g6-story (unit 2, days 19 to 32) | th-g7-story (unit 6): a scene staged two ways, the author's first production, period objects | th-g8-story (unit 10) retrieves th-g7-story (unit 6, days 83 to 96): pacing, two productions compared, objects used | Versions compared, then the author's picture and objects, then productions and pacing |
| World | th-g6-world (unit 4, days 49 to 62) | th-g7-world (unit 8): many community viewpoints, another art from the setting | th-g8-world (unit 12) retrieves th-g7-world (unit 8, days 113 to 126): a community issue in varied kinds of drama | A shared theme, then woven viewpoints, then an issue examined through several forms |
| Noticing | th-g6-notice (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | th-g7-notice (unit 5): reactions compared with a classmate's | th-g8-notice (unit 9) retrieves th-g7-notice (unit 5, days 65 to 82): decisions judged against criteria | Written, then compared, then judged |
| Judging | th-g6-judge (unit 3, days 35 to 48) | th-g7-judge (unit 7): preference backed by evidence, the aim and its audience | th-g8-judge (unit 11) retrieves th-g7-judge (unit 7, days 99 to 112): evidence, taste and criteria paired; effect judged | A judgment, then a preference, then a paired judgment of effect |

Band course days above (year 7 starts on day 65, year 8 on day 129).

### Handed on to Theater, grades 9 to 12 (Level 1)

Level 1 opens with a bridge unit that teaches the grade 8 techniques and words Level 1 needs, as readiness, and
claims no grade 8 id (STANDARD.md 3.2; th-g9-imagine's note), so a student who did not take this course still enters.

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (Level 1) | What Level 1 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| th-g8-imagine | 10 | th-g9-imagine | Research begins a production concept, tested in a concept page |
| th-g8-show | 12 | th-g9-show | The roles of a production are mapped, and a script is staged for an audience the group chooses |
| th-g8-actor | 9 | th-g9-actor | A character is built from the script's given circumstances and tested for believability |
| th-g8-design | 11 | th-g9-design | Research and technology shape the design, defended in a design folio |
| th-g8-story | 10 | th-g9-story | Relationships carry the story, and research finds its cultural and social roots |
| th-g8-world | 12 | th-g9-world | A dramaturgy page compares belief systems across cultures, places and eras |
| th-g8-notice | 9 | th-g9-notice | Criteria are drafted from the student's own response and justified |
| th-g8-judge | 11 | th-g9-judge | A written critique ties a piece to other arts, history and culture |

Each hand-on above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/arts.csv (the th-g9 rows' `assumes` cells).

